[Music]  4th of july celebrations are in full  swing and the summerlin area showed some  love for america with the annual  america's birthday party parade today  several members of our 8 news now team  also served as hosts  8 news now reporter victoria saha takes  a look  the july heat didn't stop summerlin  residents celebrating america's birthday  their annual america's birthday party  made a comeback after having to go  virtual last year i have never missed a  parade  long time residents like kathy koch  aren't alone  faith gregory has been coming to the  parade ever since it started  i love america i am such a patriot  and i have grown up in summerlin this is  actually my  16th year of the summerlin parade and  her love for the parade was  evident in her outfit and her hair she  got blue highlights just for the  occasion  so i just wanted to celebrate america's  birthday  support all of our military all of our  everything that america stands for  freedom independence and share of great  birthday  this year's parade had a shorter route  but a huge turnout  however small it is whatever it is i  know i'm going to love it  which surprised organizers didn't really  have an expectation we just wanted to  provide an event that we were very proud  of and that we thought  the community would enjoy pearl says the  parade almost didn't happen because of  the ongoing pandemic  but as soon as restrictions lifted on  june 1st he said they took action to  bring back a summerlin tradition  organizers say that they were just happy  that they were able to pull off this  parade in such a short notice  reporting from summerlin victoria saha 8  news now

